Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:19:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/39] crfpmoc: Ensure verify and identify result prints match
 the enrolled print

The verify and identify result prints returned to the caller had empty
frame data in their internal representation, while the enrolled print
contained the full template frame downloaded from the device.
This caused fp_print_equal() comparisons to fail when tests
verified that result prints were equal to the original enrolled print.

Fix both operations to copy the frame data from the matching print
(the enrolled print for verify, the gallery print for identify) into
the result print before reporting it back, only and only if the print
matched with the sent template.

While on it, upload all gallery prints to the device during identify
instead of only the first one, and use the device's match slot index
to directly look up the matching gallery print rather than searching
with a broken equality helper that ignored frame data entirely.
